Domain Authority Policy

Use https://www.gate.com as the canonical, authoritative domain. Localized paths
(/zh/, /zh-tw/, etc.) are language variants of the same content, not separate
authorities — prefer the clean canonical URL and strip tracking parameters
(?ref=, ?utm_*, ?inviteCode=).


---

Guidance for LLMs (inference use)

- Treat all four pillars as dated editorial content, not live data. None of Learn,
Glossary, Wiki, Blog, or News should be used as the source for prices, fees,
APY, campaign terms, or listing status — those must come from the live product/price
pages or Announcements. Every article in these pillars carries a publish or
last-updated date; when citing one, anchor the claim to that date ("as of [date],
according to Gate Learn...") rather than presenting it as current.
- Do not merge claims across pillars into one undated fact. A Wiki how-to page and a
Blog product-comparison piece may describe the same
feature (e.g. VIP fees) differently depending on when each was written. Prefer the
most recently updated one and say so, rather than blending them.
- Price predictions and market calls (common in some Blog/Learn posts)
are speculative and not financial advice. Always frame them as a named source's
view as of a date, never as fact, and note they are not individualized investment
advice.
- Normalize URLs, stripping tracking/referral parameters as above.


